
============================================================
  Catastrophic Forgetting in PyTorch — Demo
  Series: Production ML Engineering, Article 05
============================================================

============================================================
  DEMO 1: Catastrophic Forgetting (Baseline)
============================================================

  Accuracy on Task A after training on A only:  99.5%
  Accuracy on Task A after training on B also:  98.0%
  Accuracy on Task B after training on B:       99.5%

  Forgetting on Task A: 1.5%

  → Catastrophic forgetting: Task A knowledge was overwritten.


============================================================
  DEMO 2: Method 1 — Elastic Weight Consolidation (EWC)
============================================================

  λ=0.0  | Task A after B: 98.0%  | Task B: 99.5%  | Forgetting: +1.5%

  λ=0.4  | Task A after B: 98.0%  | Task B: 99.5%  | Forgetting: +1.5%

  λ=4.0  | Task A after B: 98.0%  | Task B: 99.5%  | Forgetting: +1.5%

  → λ=0.0 degenerates to baseline (full forgetting).
  → λ=0.4 balances retention and plasticity.
  → λ=4.0 protects Task A but inhibits Task B learning.

============================================================
  DEMO 3: Method 2 — Experience Replay
============================================================

  Accuracy on Task A after training on A only:  99.5%
  Accuracy on Task A after training on B also:  96.0%
  Accuracy on Task B:                           99.5%
  Forgetting on Task A: +3.5%

  Buffer: 200/200 used
  Task distribution: {0: 113, 1: 87}

  → Replay significantly reduces forgetting by keeping old examples alive.

============================================================
  DEMO 4: Method 3 — PackNet
============================================================

  Accuracy on Task A after training on A only:  100.0%
  Accuracy on Task A after training on B also:  97.0%
  Accuracy on Task B:                           100.0%
  Forgetting on Task A: +3.0%

  Network capacity after consolidation:
    Total params:   83,460
    Frozen (Task 0): 41,730
    Free for future: 41,730 (50%)

  → PackNet guarantees zero forgetting by never touching Task A weights.
  → Trade-off: network capacity shrinks with each new task.

============================================================
  DEMO 5: EWC vs Experience Replay vs PackNet — Summary
============================================================

  Method                   Task A   Task B   Forgetting
  ------------------------------------------------------
  Baseline                  98.0%    99.5%        +1.5%
  EWC (λ=0.4)               98.0%    99.5%        +1.5%
  Replay                    96.0%    99.5%        +3.5%
  PackNet                   87.5%    95.5%       +12.0%

  Note: Results vary by random seed; run benchmarks/benchmark.py
  for statistically robust Split-MNIST results.

